      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by 33, we first need to identify the smallest four-digit number, which is 1000. We will then check for the smallest number greater than or equal to 1000 that is divisible by 33. \n\nLet's perform the divisibility check step by step:\n\n1. We start by dividing 1000 by 33 to find the next whole number:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1000}{33} \\approx 30.303\n   \\]\n\n2. To find the smallest integer greater than or equal to 30.303, we round up to the next whole number, which is 31.\n\n3. Now, we multiply 31 by 33 to find the smallest four-digit number divisible by 33:\n   \\[\n   31 \\times 33 = 1023\n   \\]\n\nThus, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by 33 is \\boxed{1023}.\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Find the smallest four-digit number divisible by 33\nsmallest_four_digit = 1000\n\n# Find the smallest integer greater than or equal to smallest_four_digit / 33\nimport math\nnext_multiple = math.ceil(smallest_four_digit / 33) * 33\n\n# Check if it is divisible by 33\nwhile next_multiple % 33 != 0:\n    next_multiple += 33\n\nprint(next_multiple)\n```",
